A||||5||rockcrawl||Disapointing mention of the Fiero in Car Collector magazine||||13||
Z||000000||rockcrawl||05-19-2001||10:02 PM||||I was browsing through the January 2001 issue of Car Collector magazine that was part of the "goodie bag" that was handed out to all Carlisle show participants. I was excited when I came to a feature titled "The 20th Century Automoble" and saw a small picture of a Fiero among others. I quickly turned to the 1981-1990 section where there is a 1/3 page picture of an '85 GT and a caption that reads: "In the 1980's Pontiac gave us the Fiero, then <B>fortunately</B> took it away. It was a good idea that never reached its full potential before dwindling sales killed it off." <P>The guy that wrote that (Dennis Adler) must be a real idiot. If the car had not yet reached its full potential, why is it fortunate that they took it away. I don't quite understand that one. Wouldn't it have been more fortunate for them to continue production for a few more years and perfect it? Needles to say, the Fiero did not make it onto their "most desireable cars" or "100 greatest cars" list.||||reg||13
Z||000001||PBJ||05-19-2001||10:15 PM||||Typical person commenting on something he has not done any research on.  "Ohh all fieros catch fire."  "ohh all fieros have engines in the frt don't they."   "or was it the fuel tank in the frt." I bet he has never even been in one, let alone drive or own one.  But then again most of us have never just owned one or two....  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||cadaver||05-19-2001||10:23 PM||||I had mine smogged the other day. And the guy was looking and looking for the trunk release. I said do you want me to open it? He said. "No I know where it is, But I will just use the key anyway." Well then I informed him as to the fact that I dont have a key for the trunk. So I said here let ne show you. So I reached up on the dash and hit the switch. He says. "Hey why did you move it up there?" I and said that is where they are in a fiero. And he says "Since when?" So I told him they started putting them up there in these in 84 and quit putting them there in 88. <BR>You know instead of just saying Hmm I didnt know that. He still insisted that it WAS on the floor by the seat and someone moved it to the dash.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Stoic||05-19-2001||10:31 PM||||Yes, it is discouraging to hear the negativity from people, especially when it in the form of a magazine review.  Everytime I roll into my parents house for a visit I get a glare and a "coffin on wheels" comment.  They hate my car and the previous one I owned and have tried to make me sell it.  A while back I had my car on here for sale, I had been forced to borrow money from them and they said they would lend it to me on the condition that I sold my car.  So, I busted my butt and paid them back within the week and told them to mind their own business about what I drive.  Unfortunate.<P>------------------<BR>If you can read this, I'm parked.||||reg||1
Z||000004||84Bill||05-20-2001||11:36 PM||||You really wnat a piece of pathetic information? My friend took his 85 Fiero to the dealer to have the recalls done. When he went to pick it up the Manager informed him the brakes were bad and needed replacing. My friend then informed the manager the the brakes were done not more than 2 months ago and that it was not possible they were bad alredy. The manager then called in the mechanic who then gave an explanation as to why the brakes were bad, the mechanic explained that the brake light was on when he pulled it out and test drove it(approx 2 miles down and back) My friend then asked if he released the parking brake and the mechanic said the brake was not on because the lever was down. After showing the manager and the mechanic how to release the parking brake the manager offer to replace the rotors pads and calipers free of charge.<BR>good thing he took it to a Pontiac dealer!||||reg||13
Z||000005||AusFiero||05-22-2001||09:58 AM||||Come on Bill we have all heard the my this or my friend that story.<P>Own up man, wasn't your fault your got an idiot for a dealer.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero.gif"> <BR>When I was young I spent 80% of my money on Women, Gambling and Alcohol. I guess I wasted the rest.||||reg||1
